{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCpWcfGswKKbtcjtTo2f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hook doesn't return `null` for a logged-out user. It returns a `Session` whose `authenticated` flag is `false`, so callers branch on that flag.\n\n**How a component reads the session**\n\n1. A component calls `useSession()` from `@openmrs/esm-framework`, which re-exports the hook from `esm-react-utils` (`openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/index.ts:48`, `public.ts:42`). The hook is documented in `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/useSession.md`, which says it \"returns an object with property `authenticated` == `false` if the user is not logged in\" and \"will never return `null`/`undefined`.\"\n2. The hook reads a global session store (`sessionStore`, created in `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts:29-32`) through `getSessionStore()`. On the first render it throws a Suspense promise until the store reports `loaded: true`, then it subscribes to updates so components re-render on login, logout, or user changes (`openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/useSession.ts:17-116`).\n3. Consumers read `session.user` or `session.authenticated` directly. Examples: `openmrs-esm-core/packages/apps/esm-primary-navigation-app/src/components/user-panel-switcher-item/user-panel-switcher.component.tsx:6`, and in the chart `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-orders-app/src/order-favorites/useFavoritesActions.ts:20` (`const { user } = useSession()`).\n\n**What happens when nobody is authenticated**\n\n- The session endpoint answers 401 or 403 with a body like `{ authenticated: false, sessionId: '' }`. `handleSessionResponse` treats that as the answer \"not logged in\", not as an error, and stores it as a loaded, unauthenticated session (`current-user.ts:567-602`, with `isAuthFailure` at 604-606 and `isUnauthenticatedSession` at 634-636). The hook then returns that object, so `session.authenticated === false` and `session.user` is absent.\n- After a logout, `clearCurrentUser()` writes `{ loaded: true, session: { authenticated: false, sessionId: '' } }` to the store (`current-user.ts:291-299`), and `logout()` does the same after the server call (`current-user.ts:553-565`).\n- A failure that is not an auth response, with nothing loaded yet, is recorded as a store error (`recordSessionFailure`, `current-user.ts:642` onward). The hook keeps suspending, and the app shell shows an error page, as tested in `openmrs-esm-core/packages/shell/esm-app-shell/src/run.test.ts:253-260`.\n- The app shell only sets up optional dependencies once the session is authenticated (`openmrs-esm-core/packages/shell/esm-app-shell/src/events.ts:9-20`).\n- The login app sends logged-out users to the login route. `redirect-logout.component.tsx:15-25` navigates to the configured `loginUrl` for custom providers, or to `${openmrsSpaBase}/login` otherwise. `openmrs-esm-core/packages/apps/esm-login-app/src/login/login.component.tsx:104` reads the authenticated flag, but I did not read that file, so I have not verified its redirect logic.\n\n**Tests**\n\n- `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/useSession.test.tsx:22-87` covers the hook's behaviour.\n- `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.test.ts:686-701` covers the unauthenticated fetch result.\n\n**Not checked:** I used all ten search calls. I did not trace the full path from the shell's root to the login route, and the exact `refetchCurrentUser` declaration (around `current-user.ts:240`) was not read in full.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/useSession.ts\", \"startLine\": 17, \"endLine\": 116},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 567, \"endLine\": 602},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 291, \"endLine\": 299},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 604, \"endLine\": 606},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 634, \"endLine\": 636},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 553, \"endLine\": 565},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 642, \"endLine\": 656},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 29, \"endLine\": 32},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 64, \"endLine\": 74},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 76, \"endLine\": 104},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/useSession.md\", \"startLine\": 3, \"endLine\": 19},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/apps/esm-login-app/src/redirect-logout/redirect-logout.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 8, \"endLine\": 52},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/shell/esm-app-shell/src/events.ts\", \"startLine\": 9, \"endLine\": 20},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/useSession.test.tsx\", \"startLine\": 22, \"endLine\": 87},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.test.ts\", \"startLine\": 686, \"endLine\": 701},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/shell/esm-app-shell/src/run.test.ts\", \"startLine\": 234, \"endLine\": 260},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/apps/esm-login-app/src/login/login.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 104, \"endLine\": 104},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/mock.tsx\", \"startLine\": 56, \"endLine\": 58},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/apps/esm-pr